USB on spes: DWC3 at khaje addresses, opt-in with sweetusb (0170).

The CDC-ECM gadget and live UDP log of 0072-0077 worked on sweet. spes kept them off because
the addresses were SM7150's. Observed on a spesn live DT: ssusb@4e00000 (QSCRATCH at +0xf8800,
as the driver assumes), gdsc@141a004 in GCC 0x1400000, hsphy@1613000 (SNPS femto), SMMU SID 0x120;
CBCR offsets from Linux gcc-khaje.c. sweetusb=1 only reads state and reads DWC3 only with the GDSC
and clocks on; sweetusb=2 passes SID 0x120 through the SMMU (the DMA buffers are above 4 GiB)
and starts the device. Not given: USB stays off. Untested on hardware. ABL leaving the
controller clocked, in device mode with the femto PHY set up, is assumed from sweet: =1 checks it.

